config FREETZ_PACKAGE_TELLDUS
	bool "telldusd (Tellstick daemon)"
	select FREETZ_LIB_libconfuse
	select FREETZ_LIB_libftdi
	select FREETZ_LIB_libtelldus_core
	default n
	help
		telldusd is the daemon of telldus-core, the open source driver of
		the Tellstick 433 MHz transmitter/receiver. It owns the USB stick
		(Tellstick Classic or Duo, driven through libftdi) and serves the
		client library over a local socket, so that programs like Domoticz
		(its Telldus hardware type) or the tdtool command line client -
		shipped by this package - can send and receive 433 MHz codes.

		A Tellstick Duo can also receive, which is what makes it useful
		for remote controls and sensors of that frequency.

		The configuration of the known devices is stored in
		/mod/etc/conf/tellstick.conf and can be edited from the web
		interface below; devices learned at run time are written to
		/mod/etc/conf/tellstick-state.conf. Both files live in the
		persistent part of the freetz configuration framework, because
		the firmware image itself is read only.

		Web interface: http://fritz.box:81/cgi-bin/conf/telldus
		Log file: /tmp/rc.telldus.log
